Added config file support. The config file supports 200 Udbase dirs.
Also note the config file must not be over 6000 bytes. This should
be easy to do. The config follows the following format:

Title to be displayed maximum of 31 chars. (CNet limit not mine)
Actual DOS Partition (I.e. UDbase0:)
Subdir name.

This is repeated for each section. Do not add blank line(s) in the config
at any point. DO not add spaces, comments etc. Well you can use
spaces for the udbase "Title" part of the config. But not for the directory
information. I only put the config in for a quick down and dirty method 
of "having it your way". Well look at the enclosed config you should get 
the idea of what is going on. Also the config file is OPTIONAL and will 
override most flags such as access group, private subdir, alphabetical 
subdir sorts etc. Any flags having to do with bases. Also take note
that if ANY of your file sections have more than 500 files, make sure
your using the special version of TUCFGII.big.

